# Docs site sync

When you change behavior, APIs, or UX in the monorepo, update the **public documentation** in `/docs` in the same task. Do not leave docs out of date.

Internal monorepo notes (build, packages, release) belong in `/contributing` — not on docs.stream-kit.app.

## What to update

| Change | Update |
| --- | --- |
| New or changed trigger/handler | Run `pnpm generate:docs-reference` (regenerates `/docs/api/triggers` and `/docs/api/handlers`) |
| Plugin settings, pages, or capabilities | `/docs/plugins/<plugin>.mdx` |
| Actions, triggers, variables, queues, collections | Matching page under `/docs/guide/` |
| Overlay manifest, events, presets, server flow | `/docs/guide/overlays.mdx`, `/docs/developers/overlay-authoring.mdx`, and overlay plugin docs |
| New plugin or public developer workflow | `/docs/plugins/`, `/docs/developers/`, and `docs/meta.json` nav if needed |
| User-facing setup or install steps | `/docs/get-started/` |

## Triggers and handlers

Definition changes in `plugins/*/src/trigger/**` or `plugins/*/src/handler/**` (and app overlay handlers under `packages/app/src/lib/core/overlay/`) are **not** documented until you regenerate:

```bash
pnpm generate:docs-reference
```

After generator or metadata script changes, regenerate and spot-check a few generated pages (conditions, variables, configuration placeholders).

## Before finishing

1. Identify whether the change is user-visible — if yes, update `/docs` (English).
2. Regenerate API reference when triggers/handlers or generator scripts changed.
3. Fix broken MDX (brace placeholders in tables belong in backticks, not `\{…\}`).
4. Verify with `pnpm dev:docs` or `pnpm build:docs` when docs content changed.

## Examples

- Add Twitch handler `send-announcement` → regenerate API reference; optionally mention it on `/docs/plugins/twitch.mdx`.
- Change overlay event payload shape → update overlay guide + developer overlay authoring page.
- Rename a queue setting in Core → update `/docs/guide/queues.mdx` and Core plugin page if exposed in UI.
